# Rust
/target
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock is deliberately TRACKED. DRADIS is an application, not a library,
# and Cargo's own guidance is to commit the lockfile for binaries so builds are
# reproducible. It is also load-bearing for the AMI: deploy/ami/build-ami.sh
# ships `git archive HEAD`, so an untracked lockfile is simply absent from the
# build context and the Dockerfile's `COPY Cargo.toml Cargo.lock ./` fails.
# Without it, the image sold to a customer could resolve different crate
# versions than the ones tested here.

# Environment / Secrets (CRITICAL - Never commit!)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.local.example

# Personal config — users must copy an example to create their own
#src/config.rs

# Example scripts (don't commit, use .example versions for public repo)
deploy-multi.sh
logs-all.sh
status.sh
stop-all.sh
!deploy-multi.sh.example
!logs-all.sh.example
!status.sh.example
!stop-all.sh.example

# Private notes
.README
CLAUDE.md

# Docker
Dockerfile.*
# control-tower/Dockerfile is deliberately TRACKED: deploy/ami/provision.sh
# builds the Control Tower image from it on the AMI builder, and the build
# context there is `git archive HEAD`, so an ignored Dockerfile is simply not
# present and `docker build control-tower/` fails.
.dockerignore
**/.docker

# Logs & temp
logs/
*.tmp
# session.file <-- Temporarily removed this line to allow access
!session.file

# Control Tower (Next.js)
control-tower/.next/
control-tower/node_modules/
# control-tower/package-lock.json is tracked for the same reasons as Cargo.lock,
# and additionally because the Control Tower Dockerfile runs `npm ci`, which
# refuses to run at all without a lockfile.
control-tower/.env.local
control-tower/.env*.local

# Agent-generated files (see AGENTS.md for guidelines)
# Do not commit: analysis, summary, or debug documentation
_analysis.md
_debug.md
_notes.md
_summary.md
_checklist.md
_improvements.md
_improvements_*.md
_session_*.md
PROFITABILITY_IMPROVEMENTS_*.md
SESSION_MONITORING_CHECKLIST.md
CONFIG_CHANGES_APPLIED.md

